From: VLCKit Aloha Release <devnull@alohabrowser.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] apple/build.sh: neutralise _LIBCPP_ENABLE_ASSERTIONS for
 Xcode 26+

Xcode 26's libc++ removed _LIBCPP_ENABLE_ASSERTIONS (replaced by
_LIBCPP_HARDENING_MODE) and turns any `#define _LIBCPP_ENABLE_ASSERTIONS`
into a hard #error. A few contrib meson subprojects (harfbuzz->ragel-6.10,
libplacebo) still hardcode -D_LIBCPP_ENABLE_ASSERTIONS=1, so contrib
compilation aborts immediately.

Append `-U_LIBCPP_ENABLE_ASSERTIONS -D_LIBCPP_HARDENING_MODE=_LIBCPP_HARDENING_MODE_NONE`
to the flags written into contrib config.mak so they propagate to every
meson/cmake project the contrib build runs. The -U comes AFTER any
hardcoded -D in the project's own meson.build, neutralising it.
---
 extras/package/apple/build.sh | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/extras/package/apple/build.sh b/extras/package/apple/build.sh
index 0000000..1111111 100755
--- a/extras/package/apple/build.sh
+++ b/extras/package/apple/build.sh
@@ -690,7 +690,7 @@ mkdir -p "$VLC_CONTRIB_INSTALL_DIR"

 # Write config.mak with flags for the build and compiler overrides
 # Set flag to error on partial availability
-write_config_mak "-Werror=partial-availability"
+write_config_mak "-Werror=partial-availability -U_LIBCPP_ENABLE_ASSERTIONS -D_LIBCPP_HARDENING_MODE=_LIBCPP_HARDENING_MODE_NONE"

 # Write crossfile-meson with flags for the build and compiler overrides
 write_crossfile_meson
